      ":question/problem": "![](images/df/df23847ad136373b2d886680f1ba0f4168bfffa39ea347ded760193f0ae5d0fe.png)\n\nA conical glass contains water. The height of the glass is $50mm$ and the radius at the top is $10mm$. Water is evaporating from the glass at a rate of $16mm^{3}/h$. If the water height is $40mm$ at a particular moment, how fast is the water height decreasing at that moment?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
